# Status Badges

Use shared tokens from `@/shared/utils/statusBadges` for lifecycle and domain status labels. Delete/destructive **actions** use [delete-destructive-actions.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/delete-destructive-actions.mdc); status badges use the separate semantic palette below.

## Tokens

Import `statusBadgeClasses` and map domain statuses in a small feature helper (e.g. `getServiceStatusColor`), not inline Tailwind in every card:

```tsx
import { Badge } from "@/components/ui/badge";
import { statusBadgeClasses } from "@/shared/utils/statusBadges";

<Badge className={`border text-xs px-2 py-1 ${statusBadgeClasses.green}`}>
  Active
</Badge>
```

Available keys: `green`, `gray`, `yellow`, `orange`, `purple`, `blue`, `red`.

## Domain mapping

- Define `Record<YourStatus, keyof typeof statusBadgeClasses>` (or similar) in the feature utils file
- Reuse labels/colors from `STATUS_BADGE_GROUPS` when adding new statuses — keep showcase catalog in sync

## Do not

- Scatter one-off `bg-green-500/20 text-green-600` strings when a token exists
- Use status badge red for delete buttons — use destructive action colors instead
- Mix unrelated status color logic inside card JSX — centralize in utils

